=== Memory Mapping Persistence Tests ===

These tests verify fundamental mmap() behavior:
1. Mapped memory remains accessible after closing file descriptor
2. Mapped memory behavior when original file is removed

=== Test: Memory Mapping Persistence After File Descriptor Close ===

Creating test file: persistent_test.txt (284 bytes)
Test file created successfully

Phase 1: Opening file and mapping into memory
  Opened file with descriptor: 3
  File mapped successfully
  Mapped length: 284 bytes
  Verifying data access while file is open...
  SUCCESS: Data matches original content while file is open

Phase 2: Closing file descriptor
  File descriptor 3 closed
  SUCCESS: mmap still reports as mapped after fd close

Phase 3: Accessing mapped memory after file descriptor close
  Testing memory access after file descriptor close...
  SUCCESS: All mapped data still accessible and correct
  First 100 characters of mapped data:
  "This is a test file for persistent memory mapping.\nWe will map this file into memory, close the file"

  Testing byte-by-byte access to entire mapped region...
  SUCCESS: All 284 bytes accessible and correct

Phase 4: Cleanup
  Memory mapping cleaned up
  Test file removed
  Test completed successfully

=== CONCLUSION: Memory mapping persists after file descriptor close ===
This demonstrates that mmap() creates an independent mapping that
survives the closure of the original file descriptor.

=== Test: Memory Mapping After File Removal ===

Creating test file: removable_test.txt (97 bytes)
Test file created successfully

Phase 1: Mapping file with _mulle_mmap_map_file
  File mapped successfully: 97 bytes
  Initial data verification: SUCCESS

Phase 2: Removing file while mapped
  File 'removable_test.txt' removed from filesystem
  mmap still reports as mapped after file removal

Phase 3: Accessing mapped memory after file removal
  Testing memory access after file removal...
  SUCCESS: Mapped data still accessible and correct after file removal
  First 50 characters: "Test content for file removal scenario.\nThis tests"

Phase 4: Cleanup
  Memory mapping cleaned up
  Test completed

=== CONCLUSION: Memory mapping behavior with file removal ===
On most Unix systems, mapped memory survives file removal because
the kernel maintains the file data until all references are closed.

=== All Memory Mapping Persistence Tests Completed ===
